{"name":"Celluloid","hex":"#515153","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"celluloid","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a variety of thermoplastics created from nitrocellulose and camphor, once used as photographic film.","The genre of cinema; film."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celluloid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Celluloid","blocks":[{"text":"Celluloids are a class of materials produced by mixing nitrocellulose and camphor, often with added dyes and other agents. Once much more common for its use as photographic film before the advent of safer methods, celluloid's common present-day uses are for manufacturing table tennis balls, musical instruments, combs, office equipment, fountain pen bodies, and guitar picks."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celluloid","wikidata":"Q146612"},{"title":"Celluloid (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Celluloid is a 2013 Indian Malayalam-language biographical drama film co-produced, written, and directed by Kamal. It stars Prithviraj Sukumaran, Sreenivasan, Mamta Mohandas, and Chandni. The film is based on the life of J.C. Daniel, regarded as the father of Malayalam cinema, focusing on the making of his film Vigathakumaran, and the story of its heroine, P. K. Rosy. The film is particularly based on Life of J. C. Daniel, a biography of J. C. Daniel written by Chelangatt Gopalakrishnan. Filming began in November 2012, and the online posters, created by a 16-year-old boy, Aswin, which went viral on social media. Released in February 2013, the film received positive reviews and won seven Kerala State Film Awards, including Best Film and Best Actor (Prithviraj). It was also supported by All Lights Film Services (ALFS), a leading film festival consultancy and become a box-office success."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c8/Celluloid_film.jpg/330px-Celluloid_film.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celluloid_(film)","wikidata":"Q4325748"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Arco_pen.jpg/500px-Arco_pen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Arco_pen.jpg/1280px-Arco_pen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Arco_pen.jpg/500px-Arco_pen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Celluloid and sterling silver pen.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArco_pen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/US-NJ%281891%29_p568_NEWARK%2C_THE_CELLULOID_COMPANY.jpg/500px-US-NJ%281891%29_p568_NEWARK%2C_THE_CELLULOID_COMPANY.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/US-NJ%281891%29_p568_NEWARK%2C_THE_CELLULOID_COMPANY.jpg/500px-US-NJ%281891%29_p568_NEWARK%2C_THE_CELLULOID_COMPANY.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Newark, New Jersey, industrial production complex of the Celluloid Company (c. 1890)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUS-NJ(1891)_p568_NEWARK%2C_THE_CELLULOID_COMPANY.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Old_celluloid_film_rolls_%285201105455%29.jpg/500px-Old_celluloid_film_rolls_%285201105455%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Old_celluloid_film_rolls_%285201105455%29.jpg/1280px-Old_celluloid_film_rolls_%285201105455%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Old_celluloid_film_rolls_%285201105455%29.jpg/500px-Old_celluloid_film_rolls_%2852011